cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its manuscript reproducibility package, please cite the archived software release and associated manuscript."
title: "EnerMat Explorer: reproducibility package for physics-informed multi-objective screening of lead-free Sn-Ge perovskites"
version: 2.0.0
date-released: 2026-08-25
url: https://github.com/omogbadebowale/EnerMat-Explorer
repository-code: https://github.com/omogbadebowale/EnerMat-Explorer.git
license: MIT
type: software
keywords:
  - perovskites
  - photovoltaics
  - tin-germanium
  - materials screening
  - sensitivity analysis
  - reproducibility
authors:
  - family-names: Yusuf
    given-names: Gbadebo Taofeek
    orcid: https://orcid.org/0000-0002-9532-8134
abstract: >
  EnerMat Explorer v2.0.0 contains the manuscript reproducibility package for
  physics-informed multi-objective screening of 231 lead-free Sn-Ge mixed-halide
  perovskite compositions. The release includes literature-informed band-gap
  calibration, interpolation-based stability and oxidation screening proxies,
  explicit composite-score mathematics, 10,000-draw scoring-model sensitivity
  analyses, a 5,000-draw descriptor-calibration stress test, synchronized data,
  and data-derived figures. The earlier interactive Streamlit workflow is retained
  in the repository for provenance. Composition-specific DFT calculations and
  experimental validation are outside the scope of this release.
